<!--
  The themed-icon layer (Android 13+). The system tints a drawable's alpha, so anything with
  internal colour flattens to a lump; only silhouette survives. The evenOdd path keeps the mane,
  skull, and knocks the eyes and nose back out so the face still reads once everything is a
  single colour. Six spikes, 60° apart, so the mane is actually symmetric rather than merely
  close to it — the same shape rotated to each position, not six separately eyeballed ones.

  The front tufts are a second, plain-fill path rather than folded into the evenOdd one: two of
  the six spikes now land close enough to them to overlap, and evenOdd unfills anywhere crossed
  twice — merged in, that overlap would carve a bite out of both instead of just layering.
-->
